    <md:title>Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>68c546f2-967d-423e-af92-91fccffbd51a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will learn that completing the square can be used to solve any quadratic equation, including equations that involve rational numbers that are not integers.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Solve by completing the square when given a quadratic equation in which the coefficient of the squared term is 1.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>9.3.1: Solving Equations with Fractions</item>
        <item>9.3.2: Using Completing the Square to Solve Equations <list id="list-00003">
            <item>9.3.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>9.3.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>9.3.3: Solve by Completing the Square <list id="list-00004">
            <item>9.3.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>9.3.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>9.3.4: Completing the Square with Fractions</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you'll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>9.3.5: Practice</item>
        <item>9.3.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>